Cell["\<\
Projects lead onsite h0 and lead intercell h1 onto their photon-zero sector. \
Projects the CSR-to-lead coupling v onto photon zero on both sides.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->103302326,ExpressionUUID->"7a66bd0f-7ed9-fa47-804a-ce98439cb702"],

Cell["\<\
Input matrices use internal-major, photon-minor ordering, with 2 m + 1 photon \
sectors. The result is the three-element lead block list for the reduced \
space.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->627583444,ExpressionUUID->"3ffc8a9d-ab7e-1842-a0fa-bbcdb0985f25"],

Cell["\<\
Options are \"ExpansionOrder\" -> 1 and \"MicromotionCorrection\" -> False. \
The coupling correction is applied only when the order is 2 and micromotion \
correction is True; csrBlocks supplies the extended scattering-region blocks \
used by that correction.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->395215360,ExpressionUUID->"f3d84c07-d1c3-6844-96f6-ffee8468e7e4"],

Cell["\<\
The default behavior is projection. Use the effective-Hamiltonian routines \
when van Vleck corrections to the Hamiltonian blocks themselves are required.\
\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1619265173,ExpressionUUID->"97daf35e-f03d-d541-96ef-d210bdea704f"]
}, Closed]],

